gpt-5.4-mini.engagement-letter-draft:
Below is a standard client engagement letter template for a residential conveyancing matter. You may wish to adapt the firm details, regulatory wording, and any jurisdiction-specific terms before use.

---

**[FIRM NAME]**  
**[Address]**  
**[Email] | [Phone]**  

**Date:** [Insert date]

**Private and Confidential**

**Sarah Byrne**  
[Client Address]

### Re: Residential Conveyancing Matter – Purchase of 14 Oakfield Road, Galway

Dear Sarah,

We are pleased to confirm that we have been instructed to act on your behalf in relation to your proposed purchase of the property at **14 Oakfield Road, Galway**.

This letter sets out the basis on which we will act for you, together with the scope of our services, our fees, and our standard terms of business.

## 1. Scope of Work

We will provide legal services in connection with the purchase of the above property, including the following:

- reviewing the contract for sale and title documentation;
- raising and considering appropriate pre-contract enquiries and requisitions on title;
- advising you on the legal implications of the purchase documentation;
- liaising with the vendor’s solicitors, your lender (if applicable), and any other relevant third parties;
- reviewing loan documentation and dealing with mortgage-related conveyancing requirements, if you are obtaining finance;
- preparing any documentation required to complete the transaction;
- arranging for execution of documents by you;
- attending to closing of the transaction;
- submitting the application for registration of your title and mortgage, where applicable, with the Property Registration Authority;
- dealing with post-completion matters incidental to the transaction.

### Matters not included
Unless we specifically agree otherwise in writing, our engagement does **not** include:
- tax advice, including Capital Acquisitions Tax, Capital Gains Tax, or Stamp Duty advice beyond general conveyancing information;
- planning, building regulation, environmental, survey, or structural advice;
- disputes or litigation arising from the transaction;
- advice on ownership structures, trusts, or succession planning;
- tenancy, letting, or management company advice beyond what is ordinarily required for conveyancing.

If any additional work is required outside the above scope, we will discuss this with you in advance.

## 2. Fees

Our professional fee for acting in this matter is a **fixed fee of EUR 1,200 plus VAT and outlays**.

### Outlays
Outlays are expenses paid to third parties on your behalf and may include, for example:
- registration fees;
- Land Registry/PRA fees;
- searches and mapping fees;
- copy folios and filings;
- postage/courier charges;
- bank transfer fees;
- Stamp Duty and any other taxes payable in connection with the purchase;
- barrister’s fees, if a barrister is required and agreed in advance.

Outlays will be charged at cost.

### VAT
VAT will be charged on our professional fee and, where applicable, on certain disbursements in accordance with the relevant tax rules.

## 3. Payment Terms

Unless otherwise agreed:
- our invoice for fees and outlays will be rendered during the transaction and/or on completion;
- payment is due on presentation of invoice;
- we may request payment on account in advance for anticipated outlays;
- we are entitled to retain relevant documents or property deeds until our fees and outlays are paid in full, to the extent permitted by law and professional rules.

## 4. Your Responsibilities

You agree to:
- provide full and accurate instructions and all information/documents requested promptly;
- notify us immediately of any change in your contact details, financial position, or funding arrangements;
- review documents we send you and respond in a timely manner;
- ensure cleared funds are available in advance of completion for all monies required, including balance purchase price, Stamp Duty, and outlays;
- disclose any relevant issue affecting the property or your proposed ownership promptly.

## 5. Timing

We will use all reasonable efforts to progress the matter efficiently. However, completion dates are often dependent on third parties, including the vendor, lender, local authorities, and the Property Registration Authority. We cannot guarantee completion by any particular date unless specifically agreed in writing.

## 6. Conflicts of Interest and Confidentiality

We will not act where a conflict of interest prevents us from doing so. We will keep your affairs confidential except where disclosure is required by law, regulation, or with your consent.

## 7. Identification and Compliance

We are required by law and professional regulation to verify your identity and, in some cases, the source of funds used in the transaction. We may ask you to provide identification documents and supporting evidence as part of our compliance checks.

## 8. Termination

You may instruct us to cease acting at any time in writing. We may also cease to act in accordance with our professional obligations or where there is a breakdown in the solicitor-client relationship. In either case, you remain liable for fees and outlays incurred up to the date of termination.

## 9. Limitation of Engagement

Our advice is provided solely to you in relation to this transaction and may not be relied upon by any other person without our written consent.

## 10. Acceptance of Terms

By instructing us to proceed, you confirm that you have read, understood, and accepted the terms of this engagement letter.

If you are happy to proceed, please sign and return the enclosed copy of this letter.

Yours sincerely,

**[Name]**  
**[Title]**  
**[Firm Name]**

